edition 5;

module ml.spec;

// What `ml` says about itself: the flag table that drives the parser, `introspect` and `skill` (cancho docs/agent-toolbox.md
// D11), the rules of its own beside the shared catalogue, and the log records. Three tables, each written once; the schemas
// (scripts/schemas.py), the fixtures (tests/fixtures/cli.json) and the gates (tests/conformance/test_tables.py) are checked
// against them, so a flag, a rule or a log record that is in one place and not in the others fails the build.
//
// Format: entries separated by `;`, fields by `|`, so no help text holds either character.

import toolbox.describe;

// name|short|kind|role|default|help
pub fn flag_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "root||path|root||resolve FILE, --model-file, --output and --log beneath this directory, following no symbolic link, and refuse paths outside it;{{MODEL_FLAG}}plan||path|path-read||fit: a plan text file (steps and a final model line, docs/pipeline.md section 2) for a model other than constant. It is the one description of the fit: --model, --step, --task and the hyperparameter flags are then args.conflict. The canonical plan is stored in the model file;step||text|none||fit: the steps of the pipeline of a model other than constant, written verb key=value as in a plan, several separated by semicolons (ASCII 59), for example impute column=* strategy=mean then scale column=a,b kind=standard. The flag may be given once. The model line is built from --model and the hyperparameter flags;{{HYPER_FLAGS}}positive||text|none||fit, eval: the positive label of a logistic classification. fit: the label whose probability the model predicts (default: the larger of the two labels). eval: the label that precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC and log-loss are about (default: the model's own);split||text|none||fit, eval: train=F with 0 < F < 1 (at most 6 digits after the point). fit trains on the train rows and reports the held-out rows. eval scores the test rows only. The rows are chosen by the seeded train/test split of lib/metrics (--seed), the test side being ceil(n * (1 - F)) rows;seed||nat|none|0|fit, eval: the seed of --split (the stream registry, kind 4). Stored in the model file;threads||nat|none|1|fit, eval: the threads of the numeric kernels, 1 to 64 (ml.param.threads outside). No thread count changes a byte of the model file or of the answer. In eval nothing is threaded and the flag is checked and unused;proba||bool|none||predict: add the probability column (the positive label's probability) to the answer of a logistic model;task||choice:regression/classification|none|regression|what the target column is: a number to predict (regression) or a label with exactly two values (classification);target||text|none||fit: the name of the column to predict, as the header spells it;drop||text|none||columns to ignore, header names separated by commas (fit, predict, eval). A dropped column is not part of the stored schema, and its cells are not read as numbers (it may hold text, quoted fields and line breaks);float||text|none||fit: columns to read as floating point whatever their cells are, header names separated by commas. A column with an exponent, a leading or trailing point or more than 12 digits is a float without being named. A float is read to the nearest double, ties to even, by cancho-table's exact reader (pinned, not copied). On a float target the constant is the exact sum of the doubles over the count, rounded once;cat||text|none||fit: columns to read as categorical text, header names separated by commas (docs/categorical.md). Every cell of such a column is a string, compared byte for byte: no case folding, no trimming, no Unicode normalisation, and it must be well-formed UTF-8. The distinct strings of a column are kept in a dictionary sorted bytewise (the id of a string is its rank), so the result does not depend on the order of the rows or on --threads. An empty cell and a cell equal to a --na-values marker are missing. A text column that is not named here is refused (ml.input.non-numeric). The target, a dropped column and a --float column cannot be named. Until a step encodes text columns (stage 2 of issue 21) a fit with --cat reads and checks the columns and then refuses with ml.input.categorical-not-encoded;na-values||text|none||fit, with --cat: strings that mean missing in a categorical column besides the empty cell, separated by commas (so a marker holds no comma), for example NA,?. At most 64 markers of 1 to 255 bytes. A marker is compared with the whole cell, byte for byte, after unquoting. Numeric columns are not affected;max-categories||nat|none|64|fit, with --cat: the most distinct values in one categorical column, 1 to 1024. More is ml.limit.categories, at the value that passes the limit, before anything is stored for it;max-string-bytes||nat|none|255|fit, with --cat: the longest cell of a categorical column in bytes, 1 to 65536. A longer one is ml.limit.string-bytes;max-pool-bytes||nat|none|1048576|fit, with --cat: the most bytes of all the distinct categories of all the categorical columns together, 1 to 8388608. More is ml.limit.string-pool;max-cat-columns||nat|none|128|fit, with --cat: the most categorical columns, 1 to 4096. More is ml.limit.categorical-columns, before the file is read past its header;output||path|path-write||fit: where to write the model file. The directory must exist. An existing file is refused unless --overwrite;model-file||path|path-read||predict, eval: the model file to read;overwrite||bool|guard||fit: replace an existing --output. The new file is written beside it under a temporary name and renamed over it, so a reader never sees half a file;dry-run||bool|guard||fit: read, check and fit, then report what would be written (planned_actions) and exit 9, writing nothing;limit||nat|none|1000|predict: the most rows in one page of predictions, at least 1;from||nat|none|0|predict: the row to start the page at, counting data rows from 0;max-rows||nat|none|10000000|the most data rows read. More is ml.input.too-many-rows;max-columns||nat|none|4096|the most columns read. More is ml.input.too-many-columns;max-cells||nat|none|400000000|the most rows times columns. More is ml.input.too-many-cells;max-line-bytes||nat|none|1048576|the longest line read. A longer one is limit.line-too-long;max-bytes||nat|none|16777216|predict, eval: the largest model file read. A larger one is limit.input-too-large;log||path|path-write||append NDJSON records of this run to this file. Records hold counts, rule tags and hashes, never a cell, a column name or a path;log-max-bytes||nat|none|1048576|refuse to log into a file already this long (limit.log-full). The log of one run adds at most 2048 bytes;format||choice:json/text|none|json|json: one document on one line. text: a few lines for a person, errors as sentences on standard error";
}

// tag|exit|repairable|summary. The shared catalogue (toolbox.rules) has args.*, path.*, io.*, limit.line-too-long,
// limit.input-too-large, conflict.exists and path.bad-name; these are ml's own. Summaries end `Hint: ... Repair: ...`.
pub fn extra() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "args.unknown-command|2|never|the first operand is not fit, predict or eval. Hint: the verbs are fit, predict and eval, and ml introspect and ml skill describe them. Repair: none.;ml.param.out-of-range|2|never|a numeric flag is below its minimum or above its ceiling. Hint: the range is in detail and in introspect limits. Repair: none.;ml.input.empty|8|never|the file has a header and no data rows. Hint: give a file with at least one data row. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-rows|8|never|more data rows than --max-rows. Hint: raise --max-rows up to its ceiling, or fit on a sample of the rows. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-columns|8|never|more columns than --max-columns. Hint: raise --max-columns up to its ceiling, or drop columns with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.input.too-many-cells|8|never|rows times columns is more than --max-cells. Hint: raise --max-cells up to its ceiling, or use fewer rows or columns. Repair: none.;ml.input.non-numeric|8|sometimes|a cell of a kept column is not a number, or is empty. A number is an integer, a decimal, or a float (an exponent, a leading or trailing point, more than 12 digits). A non-zero cell that would read as zero, and a cell longer than 1100 bytes, are refused with this tag. The line, the column and the reason are in detail. Hint: drop the column with --drop, or fix the cell. A text column the model should keep is declared with --cat (fit). Repair: retry.;ml.input.non-finite|8|never|a cell is nan or inf, or a number past the range of a double. Hint: remove the row or the column. Repair: none.;ml.input.duplicate-column|8|never|two columns have the same header name, or a column name is empty. Hint: rename the columns in the file. Repair: none.;ml.input.unknown-column|3|never|--target or --drop names a column that is not in the header. Hint: names are compared exactly, byte for byte. Repair: none.;parse.csv-ragged-row|8|never|a data row has a different number of fields from the header. The line is in detail. Hint: fix the row. Repair: none.;parse.csv-bad-quote|8|never|a closing quote is followed by something other than a comma or the end of the record. The line is in detail. Hint: double a quote that is text, or put the comma after the closing quote. Repair: none.;parse.csv-unterminated-quote|8|never|a quoted field is still open at the end of the file. The line where its record began is in detail. Hint: close the quote, or double the quotes that are text. Repair: none.;ml.label.single-class|8|never|a classification target has one value. Hint: a model needs both classes in the training rows. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-binary|8|never|a classification target has more than two values. Hint: only two-class targets are built. Repair: none.;ml.label.not-integer|8|never|a classification target is not an integer column. Hint: label the classes with integers. Repair: none.;ml.schema.mismatch|8|sometimes|the input columns differ from the fitted schema: missing, extra or of another type. They are named in detail. Hint: the missing columns must be added. Extra columns can be ignored with --drop. Repair: retry.;ml.model.bad-magic|8|never|the file does not start with CML1. Hint: this is not a cancho-ml model file. Repair: none.;ml.model.version|8|never|the file has a format version this reader does not know, or a model of kind 4 to 7 made with a summation order this reader does not implement (sum_order and known in detail). Hint: refit with this version of ml. Repair: none.;ml.model.truncated|8|never|the file ends before the end the header and the section lengths promise, or a length runs past the end. Hint: copy the file again. Repair: none.;ml.model.checksum|8|never|the SHA-256 at the end of the file is not the hash of the bytes before it. Hint: the file changed after it was written. Repair: none.;ml.metric.undefined|8|never|the sum of squared errors of a float regression is beyond the largest double. Hint: scale the target down. Repair: none.;ml.model.malformed|8|never|the file passes the checksum but a section is not what the format allows. The section is in detail. Hint: refit. Repair: none.;limit.log-full|8|never|the --log file is already --log-max-bytes long. Hint: move the log away, or raise --log-max-bytes. Repair: none.;ml.linalg.not-positive-definite|8|never|a Cholesky pivot is not above 2^-40 times its own diagonal element (dependent or nearly dependent columns, or not positive, NaN included). Hint: set l2 above 2^-40 times the diagonal (n for standardised features), drop one of the dependent columns, or centre and scale the columns. Repair: none.;ml.param.threads|2|never|a thread count outside 1 to 64, or a tree fit whose thread copies would not fit the memory ceiling. Hint: give a thread count of 1 to 64. Repair: none.;ml.fit.non-finite|8|never|a coefficient, a loss or a gain became non-finite during a fit. Hint: scale the features, add l2, or use fewer iterations. Repair: none.;ml.split.empty-fold|8|never|k is larger than the number of rows, or a train/test split would leave a side empty. Hint: use fewer folds or a smaller test size. Repair: none.;ml.fit.all-missing|8|never|a selected column has no non-missing cell in the training rows (every transform but impute strategy=constant). Hint: drop the column, or impute with a constant. Repair: none.;ml.limit.categories|8|never|a column has more distinct values than max-categories. Hint: raise max-categories up to 1024, or bucket the column. Repair: none.;ml.limit.string-bytes|8|never|a cell of a categorical column (--cat) is longer than --max-string-bytes. The line, the column, the length and the limit are in detail. Hint: raise --max-string-bytes up to 65536, or drop the column. Repair: none.;ml.limit.string-pool|8|never|the distinct categories of all the categorical columns together would take more than --max-pool-bytes. The line, the column, the size and the limit are in detail. Hint: raise --max-pool-bytes up to 8388608, or drop a column with long or many categories. Repair: none.;ml.limit.categorical-columns|8|never|more columns are named by --cat than --max-cat-columns. Seen at the header, before any row. Hint: raise --max-cat-columns up to 4096, or name fewer columns. Repair: none.;ml.input.invalid-utf8|8|never|a cell of a categorical column (--cat) is not well-formed UTF-8: an overlong form, a surrogate, a code point past U+10FFFF or a truncated sequence. The line, the column, the name and the offset of the first bad byte in the cell are in detail. Hint: re-encode the file as UTF-8 (for Latin-1 text: iconv -f latin1 -t utf-8), or remove the column from --cat and drop it. Repair: none.;ml.input.categorical-not-encoded|8|never|a column named by --cat was read and checked and no step reads text columns yet, so the fit would drop it silently. The names, the number of categories of each and the SHA-256 of the canonical dump of the vocabulary are in detail. Hint: name the column in an encode step (encode column=NAME kind=onehot), which reads text columns from stage 2 of issue 21, or remove it from --cat and drop it with --drop. Repair: none.;ml.input.unknown-category|8|never|an encode step with unknown=refuse met a value no training row had. Hint: refit with the value in the training rows, or use unknown=ignore. Repair: none.;ml.plan.syntax|8|never|a plan line is not verb key=value (line and column are in detail). Hint: one step per line, verb key=value. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-step|8|never|the verb of a plan line is not impute, scale, encode, bucket or model. Hint: use one of the five verbs. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-key|8|never|a key the verb does not take. Hint: see the keys of the verb in docs/pipeline.md. Repair: none.;ml.plan.missing-key|8|never|a required key of the verb is absent. Hint: add the key. Repair: none.;ml.plan.bad-value|8|never|a value that is not in the key's list or not a number of the key's kind. Hint: see the values of the key in docs/pipeline.md. Repair: none.;ml.plan.duplicate-key|8|never|the same key twice on one line. Hint: write each key once. Repair: none.;ml.plan.model-line|8|never|the plan has no model line, two, or a step after it. Hint: end the plan with exactly one model line. Repair: none.;ml.plan.unknown-column|8|never|a column named by a step is not a column of the matrix the step receives. Hint: names are compared byte for byte. Repair: none.;ml.limit.plan|8|never|the plan has more bytes, lines or listed columns than the limits. Hint: at most 64 KiB, 64 lines, 4096 names in a list. Repair: none.;ml.input.missing-value|8|sometimes|a feature cell is empty and no impute step of the plan covers its column (the columns are in detail). Hint: add an impute step for the columns, for example impute column=a,b strategy=mean. Repair: retry when no plan or step was given.;ml.plan.model-not-built|8|never|the model line of the plan names a model ml does not build (kmeans, tree, forest, or constant). Hint: use linear or logistic in a plan, or --model constant without one. Repair: none.";
}

// The rules of the libraries that no input can make `ml` answer (docs/wiring.md section 5): descriptors the wiring builds from a validated shape
// (ml.tensor.*), a triangular solve the relative pivot test never lets reach a zero (ml.linalg.singular), metrics given arrays of one length and
// probabilities in [0, 1] by construction (ml.metric.length-mismatch, bad-probability), trees and the stratified split (not wired). Same convention as
// extra(). They are NOT in rules(), so not in `introspect`, in the schemas or among the fixtures: a rule in the table is a promise that a fixture
// reaches it. The tags the verbs can reach moved to extra() and rules() at the wiring stage (docs/integration.md). The tags of the libraries that ml does reach (ml.input.*, ml.label.*, ml.schema.mismatch, ml.model.*,
// ml.metric.undefined, ml.param.out-of-range) are in extra() already. scripts/check_registry.py compares this table with the libraries'
// tag tables (lib/core/refuse.cho, lib/metrics/rules.cho, lib/models/tree/deny.cho) and with design.md section 8.
pub fn pending() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "ml.tensor.rank|8|never|a tensor of rank 0 or above 4 was given to a kernel. Hint: use a tensor of rank 1 to 4 (rank 1 and 2 have kernels). Repair: none.;ml.tensor.shape|8|never|an extent below 1, or a reshape of a tensor that is not contiguous. Hint: give every extent as an integer of at least 1, and reshape only a contiguous tensor to the same element count. Repair: none.;ml.tensor.bounds|8|never|the offset, shape and strides of a descriptor reach outside the data given beside it. Hint: they must stay inside the data. Repair: none.;ml.linalg.singular|8|never|a zero on the diagonal of a triangular solve. Hint: the matrix has no inverse. Repair: none.;ml.limit.depth|8|never|a tree over the depth ceiling. Hint: give a max-depth of at most 30. Repair: none.;ml.limit.nodes|8|never|a forest over the node ceiling. Hint: raise --max-nodes, lower the depth or the number of trees, or raise min-samples-leaf. Repair: none.;ml.metric.length-mismatch|8|never|two arrays of a metric have different lengths. Hint: give one prediction per row. Repair: none.;ml.metric.bad-probability|8|never|a probability outside 0 to 1. Hint: log-loss needs the probability of the positive class. Repair: none.;ml.split.stratum-too-small|8|never|a class has fewer rows than k. Hint: use fewer folds. Repair: none.";
}

// the rules ml can emit: the shared ones it reaches, then its own (extra)
pub fn rules() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "args.unknown-flag;args.missing-value;args.bad-value;args.unexpected-value;args.duplicate-flag;args.conflict;args.missing-operand;args.required-flag;args.too-many-operands;args.unknown-command;path.empty;path.dotdot;path.absolute;path.outside-root;path.too-long;path.symlink;path.bad-name;io.not-found;io.not-a-directory;io.is-a-directory;io.permission-denied;io.read-failed;io.write-failed;conflict.exists;limit.line-too-long;limit.input-too-large;limit.log-full;ml.param.out-of-range;ml.input.empty;ml.input.too-many-rows;ml.input.too-many-columns;ml.input.too-many-cells;ml.input.non-numeric;ml.input.non-finite;ml.input.duplicate-column;ml.input.unknown-column;parse.csv-ragged-row;parse.csv-bad-quote;parse.csv-unterminated-quote;ml.label.single-class;ml.label.not-binary;ml.label.not-integer;ml.metric.undefined;ml.schema.mismatch;ml.model.bad-magic;ml.model.version;ml.model.truncated;ml.model.checksum;ml.model.malformed;ml.linalg.not-positive-definite;ml.param.threads;ml.fit.non-finite;ml.split.empty-fold;ml.fit.all-missing;ml.limit.categories;ml.limit.string-bytes;ml.limit.string-pool;ml.limit.categorical-columns;ml.input.invalid-utf8;ml.input.categorical-not-encoded;ml.input.unknown-category;ml.plan.syntax;ml.plan.unknown-step;ml.plan.unknown-key;ml.plan.missing-key;ml.plan.bad-value;ml.plan.duplicate-key;ml.plan.model-line;ml.plan.unknown-column;ml.limit.plan;ml.input.missing-value;ml.plan.model-not-built";
}

// the flags each verb takes, comma separated. A flag of the table that a verb does not list is args.conflict with that verb;
// every flag of the table is listed by at least one verb (tests/conformance/test_tables.py).
pub fn allowed(verb: int) -> [] &static [byte] {
    if verb == 1 {
        return "root,model,task,target,drop,float,cat,na-values,max-categories,max-string-bytes,max-pool-bytes,max-cat-columns,output,overwrite,dry-run,plan,step{{HYPER_ALLOW}},positive,split,seed,threads,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    if verb == 2 {
        return "root,model-file,drop,limit,from,proba,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
    }
    return "root,model-file,drop,positive,split,seed,threads,max-rows,max-columns,max-cells,max-line-bytes,max-bytes,log,log-max-bytes,format";
}

// event|fields. The records of the NDJSON log (--log). Each is one line, a closed object; a field is a count, a flag, a
// rule tag or a hash, never data. `seq` is the position in the run.
pub fn log_table() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "start|event,seq,command,version;read|event,seq,rows,columns,bytes;write|event,seq,bytes,sha256;end|event,seq,ok,exit,rule";
}

// name|default|ceiling
pub fn limits() -> [] &static [byte] {
    return "limit|1000|1000000;from|0|1000000000;max-rows|10000000|1000000000;max-columns|4096|8192;max-cells|400000000|1099511627776;max-line-bytes|1048576|16777216;max-bytes|16777216|268435456;log-max-bytes|1048576|1073741824;max-categories|64|1024;max-string-bytes|255|65536;max-pool-bytes|1048576|8388608;max-cat-columns|128|4096{{LIMITS_HYPER}}";
}

pub fn tool() -> [] describe.Tool {
    return describe.Tool { name: "ml", version: "0.1.0", summary: "Fit, apply and score a model on a CSV file, with the refusals of a tool an agent can read. Models: {{MODEL_LIST}}. constant is the baseline: for a regression the training mean, for a classification the majority class and its probability. linear (least squares, ridge with --l2) and logistic (Newton's method) are fitted through a pipeline of steps (impute, scale, encode, bucket) given by --step or --plan, fitted on the training rows and stored with the estimator in ONE model file, so predict and eval apply exactly the fitted steps and there is no way to predict with another transformation. fit reads a CSV (integer, decimal and floating-point columns, RFC 4180 quoting; an empty cell is a missing value that the plan must impute) and writes a model file (CML1: sections, tensor records, a SHA-256 trailer). predict applies the stored schema, steps and model to another CSV (--proba adds the probability of a logistic model). eval scores a model on a CSV: for constant, accuracy from exact counts or the exact sum of squared errors with the RMSE; for linear, RMSE, MAE and R2; for logistic, accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC and log-loss (the positive label is --positive). --split train=F --seed N holds rows out by the seeded split of the metrics library; --threads N sets the threads of fit and changes no byte. The same input, plan and seed give the same model bytes at any thread count. Every refusal is a rule tag with its hint. Verbs: fit FILE (--target, --output; --model, --plan, --step, --l2, --iterations, --positive, --split, --seed, --threads, --task, --drop, --float, --cat, --na-values, --overwrite, --dry-run), predict FILE (--model-file; --proba, --drop, --limit, --from), eval FILE (--model-file; --positive, --split, --seed, --threads, --drop). The first operand is the verb, the second the CSV file.", usage: "fit:     ml [--root DIR] [--model {{MODEL_CHOICES}}] [--plan PLAN | --step STEPS] [--l2 X] [--iterations N] [--positive LABEL] [--split train=F] [--seed N] [--threads N] [--task regression|classification] --target NAME --output MODEL [--drop NAMES] [--float NAMES] [--overwrite] [--dry-run] [--max-rows N] [--max-columns N] [--max-cells N] [--max-line-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] fit FILE\npredict: ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--proba] [--drop NAMES] [--limit N] [--from N] [--max-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] predict FILE\neval:    ml [--root DIR] --model-file MODEL [--positive LABEL] [--split train=F] [--seed N] [--threads N] [--drop NAMES] [--max-bytes N] [--log FILE] [--format json|text] eval FILE\n\nFILE: a CSV with a header row, comma separated, RFC 4180 quoting, a byte order mark, CRLF and blank lines read. Cells are integers, decimals or floating-point numbers; nan and inf are refused; an empty cell is refused by constant and is a missing value for the pipeline models (impute it). Paths are relative to --root when given.", output: "document", schema: "ml.v1", flags: flag_table(), operands: "VERB|none|1|1|fit, predict or eval;FILE|path-read|1|1|the CSV file to read, a path relative to --root when given (absolute paths, .. and symbolic links are refused), whose first row is the header", rules: rules(), extra_rules: extra(), limits: limits(), reversibility: "irreversible-bounded", stdin: "no", guarantees: "deterministic;idempotent;dry_run" };
}
